  "response_text": "The stack allocation method defined memory as a fixed-size region and used the initial value of the Main Stack Pointer (MSP) as a reference point. The Process Stack Pointer (PSP) was assigned by subtracting 0x400 bytes from the MSP value, creating a non-overlapping region in lower memory. This approach aligns with the downward growth of stacks in ARM architecture. Knowledge of the MSP\u2019s initial location ensures the PSP is placed in valid memory, preventing conflicts or access violations. Without this reference, improper stack allocation could result in undefined behavior or system faults.\\n",
